Error Detection & Correction

Objective
This project demonstrates error detection using **Parity Bit** and **Checksum** in Python.

Features
- Converts text into binary
- Generates a parity bit
- Simulates transmission errors by flipping one bit
- Detects errors using parity and checksum
- Displays whether the message is **OK** or **ERROR DETECTED**

 Conclusion
Parity bit is simple and detects single-bit errors, while checksum is more reliable for detecting data corruption.

**Language Used:** Python 3
